Subject: District 17 Boys Soccer Awards Meeting

Hello Coaches:

Congratulations on another soccer season and good luck in the playoffs. I w=
as asked to be District 17 chair this season and am tasked with holding the=
 District Awards meeting. Typically, we hold the district meeting on Sunday=
 evening after districts and I hope to conduct ours on Sunday, 10/25 at 7 p=
m via Zoom. It should only take 20-30 minutes.

Information:

For players to be eligible for All-District recognition, as well as All-Reg=
ion and All-State, they must be entered into the system before the meeting =
begins. Please visit www.mihssca.com<http://www.mihssca.com/> to register a=
nd set-up your team profile for the current fall season if you haven=92t al=
ready done so. There is no need to enter your entire roster into the system=
, just the players you think have earned at least All-District recognition.=
 In addition to the District coach of the year, we will select our 3 All Di=
strict GKs first, top 5 defenders, and then the 24 field players. Keepers, =
top 5 defenders, and the top 12 field players will advance to the All-Regio=
n meeting. If a player makes the All-Region team, they are guaranteed to be=
 at least All-State Honorable Mention.

Please confirm that you received this message and that Sunday evening, Octo=
ber 25 at 7 works. I will follow up with the Zoom meeting information after=
 I receive confirmations. Please also let me know if you have any questions=
 about the process. Thanks!

-Charlie Hill
Head Coach
Marquette Boys Varsity Soccer



